def table(rows, widths=None):
    data=[[Paragraph(str(c), styles['CellBoldGM'] if i==0 else styles['CellGM']) for c in row] for i,row in enumerate(rows)]
    t=Table(data, colWidths=widths, repeatRows=1, hAlign='LEFT')
    t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#224f41')),('ROWBACKGROUNDS',(0,1),(-1,-1),[colors.HexColor('#f0f5f1'),colors.white]),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),6),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),6),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),6),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),6),('LINEBELOW',(0,0),(-1,0),0.5,colors.HexColor('#224f41'))]))
    story.append(t); story.append(Spacer(1,8))
def page(): story.append(PageBreak())
def footer(canvas,doc):
    canvas.setFont('Arial',8); canvas.setFillColor(colors.HexColor('#668277')); canvas.drawString(42,28,'GOODMILES  |  Working assumptions, November 2026'); canvas.drawRightString(doc.pagesize[0]-42,28,str(doc.page))

p('GOODMILES','TitleGM')
p('Model evolution & pilot economics','HeadingGM')
p('Service design, worker pay, capacity and cost breakdowns - in the order the model changed.')
p('<b>Planning context:</b> Apartment communities in Bengaluru; intended launch in December 2026. Initial funding discussed: ₹50,000. The founder later clarified an initial goal of 20 customers in the first one or two months and at least 50 by month six. These are targets, not confirmed bookings.')
p('This document records the alternatives discussed; earlier figures are not the current model. All prices, costs, service times, staffing terms and capacity figures remain assumptions for pilot validation. Figures represent a 30-day membership cycle, with 26 working days used for capacity planning.')
h('Reading the economics')
p('<b>Direct service costs</b> cover the draft allowances for products, laundry, towels and consumables. <b>Contribution</b> is revenue less stated direct costs; it is not profit. The illustrative surplus also deducts the budgeted overheads, but excludes owner pay, taxes, payment fees, depreciation, financing, additional equipment, unbudgeted insurance, employer costs and other omissions. A reserve is a budget allowance, not necessarily an actual expense.')
h('Source and scope')
p('The final GOODMILES Operating Model and Pilot Plan is the starting point. The previous Veyra documents were superseded. This report captures the subsequent discussion through the part-time worker option; it deliberately excludes the three-year plan.')
page()
h('1. Final draft: original service plans')
table([['Plan','30-day price','Included service','Direct cost','Contribution'],['INTRO','₹1,799','8 exterior visits; 2 basic interiors during visits','₹420','₹1,379'],['PLUS','₹2,799','12 exterior visits; 3 enhanced interiors; 3 tyre dressings; 2 Flex Credits','₹630','₹2,169'],['ELITE','₹3,999','16 exterior visits; 4 enhanced interiors; deep clean, sealant, concierge; 4 Flex Credits','₹1,290','₹2,709']], [65,65,230,65,70])
p('Flex Credits give priority access to alternative slots, not extra washes. The draft also proposes separately priced one-time services: exterior ₹399; basic interior add-on ₹299; standalone interior ₹599; enhanced add-on ₹399; express refresh ₹249; tyre dressing ₹99; sealant from ₹399; deep interior from ₹1,499; concierge from ₹199. These are draft prices, not verified sales.')
h('Original timing and cost assumptions')
table([['Service','Time','Variable cost'],['Exterior','30 min','₹45'],['Exterior + interior','50 min','₹75'],['Deep interior','120 min','₹300'],['Sealant','30 min','₹100'],['Concierge administration','20 min','₹50']], [240,120,135])
p('Original plan times: INTRO 280 min, PLUS 420 min and ELITE 730 min per cycle. Contribution per service hour: approximately ₹295, ₹310 and ₹223 respectively. The draft uses one employee, a split shift, 26 days, 300 productive minutes per day and an initial 80% booking limit of 6,240 minutes per month.')
h('Original 14-customer example')
table([['Mix','Revenue','Direct costs','Contribution','Service time'],['5 INTRO, 6 PLUS, 3 ELITE','₹37,786','₹9,750','₹28,036','6,110 min']],[160,85,85,85,80])
p('After the ₹27,000 fixed budget, the illustrative surplus is ₹1,036. Fixed budget: salary ₹19,000; staff/leave ₹1,000; marketing ₹1,500; phone/software ₹500; repairs ₹1,500; contingency ₹3,500. This is near break-even and nearly fills the initial booking limit.')
page()
h('2. Change: ₹400 per car per month')
p('The first commission alternative replaced the ₹19,000 salary with ₹400 per active car, while retaining the other ₹8,000 of monthly allowances and reserves. No change to service scope or direct costs was assumed.')
table([['14-customer example','Original salary','₹400 per car'],['Revenue','₹37,786','₹37,786'],['Direct service costs','₹9,750','₹9,750'],['Worker pay','₹19,000','₹5,600'],['Other allowances and reserves','₹8,000','₹8,000'],['Illustrative surplus','₹1,036','₹14,436']], [245,125,125])
p('At the original plan times, the ₹400 payment equals about ₹86 per productive service hour for INTRO, ₹57 for PLUS and ₹33 for ELITE. It pays the same per car despite different workloads. At the 14-customer capacity example, ₹5,600 is unlikely to be a viable standalone payment for the original roster.')
p('For the same 14-customer mix, after direct costs and the remaining ₹8,000 budget, ₹20,036 is available for worker pay and surplus. That implies an average ceiling of ₹1,431 per car at break-even, ₹1,074 for a ₹5,000 surplus, or ₹717 for a ₹10,000 surplus. These are arithmetic ceilings, not recommended wages.')
h('3. Change: pay by service performed')
p('First proposed schedule: ₹60 per exterior visit, plus ₹50 for an interior session; deep clean ₹300, sealant ₹60 and concierge ₹40. The PLUS tyre-dressing payment was assumed included in the exterior rate. Basic and enhanced interiors were paid the same pending timing validation.')
table([['Per customer','INTRO','PLUS','ELITE'],['Subscription','₹1,799','₹2,799','₹3,999'],['Worker pay','₹580','₹870','₹1,560'],['Direct service costs','₹420','₹630','₹1,290'],['Left before fixed costs','₹799','₹1,299','₹1,149']],[180,105,105,105])
p('For 5 INTRO, 6 PLUS and 3 ELITE: revenue ₹37,786; direct costs ₹9,750; worker pay ₹12,800; other budget ₹8,000; illustrative surplus ₹7,236.')
p('A higher comparison schedule of ₹90 per exterior, ₹75 per interior, ₹450 per deep clean, ₹90 per sealant and ₹60 per concierge produced ₹19,200 in worker pay and ₹836 in surplus for that 14-customer mix. Both schedules are proposed assumptions, not verified wage rates.')
page()
h('4. Change: 20 customers, 4:5:1 mix')
p('The 20-customer example used 8 INTRO, 10 PLUS and 2 ELITE customers, with the ₹60 / ₹50 service-payment schedule.')
table([['Plan','Customers','Revenue','Direct costs','Worker pay'],['INTRO','8','₹14,392','₹3,360','₹4,640'],['PLUS','10','₹27,990','₹6,300','₹8,700'],['ELITE','2','₹7,998','₹2,580','₹3,120'],['Total','20','₹50,380','₹12,240','₹16,460']],[95,70,110,110,110])
p('After ₹8,000 in other budgeted costs, surplus = ₹13,680. At the original service times, the mix required 7,900 minutes, above the draft’s 6,240-minute initial booking limit and its 7,800-minute theoretical service capacity. Additional capacity would have been required.')
p('At the higher ₹90 / ₹75 schedule, worker pay would be ₹24,690 and the illustrative surplus ₹5,450, before extra staffing or equipment costs.')
h('5. Change: shorter service times and six-hour day')
p('The next assumption was 15 minutes for an exterior wash and 30 minutes total for exterior plus interior. A six-hour day gives 360 minutes; reserving 20% for non-service work leaves 288 bookable minutes per day. On 26 days that is 7,488 minutes per month. These are planning assumptions, not measured results.')
table([['Visits per car per month','Exterior only','Exterior + interior'],['4','124','62'],['8','62','31'],['12','41','20'],['16','31','15']],[210,140,145])
p('The table shows mathematical ceilings for a single plan at 80% booking, rounded down. Daily slot demand, access and travel can reduce capacity. Under the 20-customer 4:5:1 example, 216 exterior visits plus 54 interiors, two deep cleans, two sealants and two concierge jobs required 4,390 minutes using the revised exterior/interior times and original add-on times.')
page()
h('6. Change: only exterior and combined care')
p('ELITE and add-ons were removed. INTRO retains 8 exterior visits with interior on 2 visits; PLUS retains 12 exterior visits with interior on 3. The customer mix becomes 40% INTRO and 60% PLUS. At 15 minutes exterior and 30 minutes combined, INTRO takes 150 minutes and PLUS 225 minutes per customer per month. The weighted average is 195 minutes: 7,488 / 195 gives a theoretical planning ceiling of about 38 customers. A suggested pilot range was 30-35.')
h('35-customer example at 15 / 30 minutes')
table([['Per 30-day cycle','14 INTRO','21 PLUS','Total'],['Revenue','₹25,186','₹58,779','₹83,965'],['Direct service costs','₹5,880','₹13,230','₹19,110'],['Worker pay','₹8,120','₹18,270','₹26,390'],['Contribution after both costs','₹11,186','₹27,279','₹38,465']],[195,100,100,100])
p('Less ₹8,000 in other budgeted expenses and reserves = ₹30,465 illustrative surplus. Service time: 6,825 minutes per month. The draft’s ₹630 PLUS direct cost includes a provisional tyre-dressing allowance, so keeping the full amount after removing tyre dressing may be conservative; its separate amount is unknown.')
h('7. Change: 20-minute exterior, 40-minute combined')
p('The 40 minutes is the total combined appointment, not 40 minutes added to the exterior. INTRO now requires 200 minutes per month; PLUS requires 300. At the 40:60 mix, average service time is 260 minutes per customer. The 7,488-minute booking allowance supports about 28 customers as a ceiling; 24-26 was suggested initially. The previous 35-customer mix requires 9,100 minutes and is not a practical one-worker schedule.')
h('28-customer example at 20 / 40 minutes')
table([['Per 30-day cycle','11 INTRO','17 PLUS','Total'],['Revenue','₹19,789','₹47,583','₹67,372'],['Direct service costs','₹4,620','₹10,710','₹15,330'],['Worker pay','₹6,380','₹14,790','₹21,170'],['Contribution after both costs','₹8,789','₹22,083','₹30,872']],[195,100,100,100])
p('Less ₹8,000 other budget = ₹22,872 illustrative surplus. The mix uses 7,300 service minutes. Direct cost allowances are unchanged despite the revised timing and must be validated.')
page()
h('8. Change: pilot salary guarantee')
p('An initial suggestion was a ₹19,000 monthly guarantee, with the worker paid the higher of that guarantee or service-based earnings. This was a comparison, not an accepted final salary: the founder considered ₹19,000 too high and proposed part-time shifts instead.')
table([['Customers','Mix INTRO / PLUS','Revenue','Direct cost','Pay with guarantee','Other budget','Surplus'],['10','4 / 6','₹23,990','₹5,460','₹19,000','₹8,000','−₹8,470'],['20','8 / 12','₹47,980','₹10,920','₹19,000','₹8,000','₹10,060'],['25','10 / 15','₹59,975','₹13,650','₹19,000','₹8,000','₹19,325'],['28','11 / 17','₹67,372','₹15,330','₹21,170','₹8,000','₹22,872']],[55,75,75,70,85,65,70])
h('9. Change: part-time shifts or different workers')
p('The founder proposed one worker taking another job between shifts, or separate workers for the morning and evening. The discussed starting estimate was ₹6,000-₹8,000 per person per month for one three-hour shift, with ₹7,000 used as a test offer. Two separate shifts therefore imply ₹14,000 in combined minimum guarantees. This is a hiring estimate, not an established wage or a promise accepted by a worker.')
p('Proposed rule: each worker receives the higher of their own ₹7,000 guarantee or the ₹60-per-exterior plus ₹50-per-interior payments for work they personally complete. This is not a guarantee plus commission. Calculate it separately for each worker; uneven shifts can require top-ups.')
table([['Customers','Revenue','Direct costs','Worker pay','Other budget','Surplus'],['10','₹23,990','₹5,460','₹14,000','₹8,000','−₹3,470'],['20','₹47,980','₹10,920','At least ₹15,080','₹8,000','Up to ₹13,980'],['28','₹67,372','₹15,330','At least ₹21,170','₹8,000','Up to ₹22,872']],[55,88,82,112,78,80])
p('The 10-customer row assumes each shift receives its ₹7,000 guarantee. The 20- and 28-customer results are upper estimates because individual worker top-ups could raise the total. Both shifts must be covered for the six-hour capacity calculation; one three-hour worker has roughly half that capacity.')
page()
h('Pilot decisions and figures to validate')
p('• Confirm which plan inclusions and prices will be sold, and publish clear scheduling, expiry and missed-visit rules.<br/>• Time actual exterior and combined visits, including quality checks. Record movement, setup, delays and rework separately. Validate that the split shifts match vehicle availability.<br/>• Measure chemicals, laundry and equipment costs per visit. The old PLUS allowance may include a removed tyre-dressing cost.<br/>• Recruit for the exact shift and location; confirm worker pay, attendance expectations, cover and how work is allocated. Check applicable Karnataka wage and employment requirements for the actual arrangement.<br/>• Build a month-by-month cash plan for the ₹50,000 starting fund, including setup, guarantees, collections, additional teams and the timing of expansion. The operating surpluses in this report do not establish that ₹50,000 is sufficient.<br/>• Count paid active customers and track renewals, on-time completion, complaints and actual contribution; expand only when the work can be reliably delivered.')
h('References')
p('GOODMILES Operating Model and Pilot Plan, founder review draft, November 2026 (user-provided PDF). Subsequent plan changes and scenarios are based on the founder’s instructions and calculations in this conversation. The earlier Veyra and apartment-car-care handoff documents informed initial discussion but were superseded by the final GOODMILES draft.','SmallGM')
p('Part-time wage estimate was informed by advertised Bengaluru job data, not a like-for-like wage survey: betterjobs.in/car-washer-salary-in-bengaluru/ and in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=b4621546520c5498. Check current applicable legal requirements and local recruitment conditions before making an offer.','SmallGM')
